    apply: "Write a list of the things that worry you most, and turn each one into a prayer with thanks, as Paul describes in Philippians 4:6. Keep the list and note any answers or any peace that comes. Offer short prayers during the day, such as when you start work or meet someone.",
    activity: "Give learners cards on which to write one worry and one thing for which they are thankful. In pairs they swap cards and pray for each other's worry and thank God for the other's blessing. Afterwards, read Philippians 4:6-7 together and discuss what changes when we pray.",
    takeHome: "Read Philippians 4:4-9, Jeremiah 33:1-9, James 4:1-10 and Luke 5:12-16. List the reasons for prayer you find. Choose one worry to pray about daily this week.",
