    teacher: "Learners may have disappointments in prayer and may be sceptical. Listen without defensiveness and avoid giving formulas. Affirm that God invites our prayers and does not demand perfection. Return to this question in later lessons on unanswered prayer.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners to give three reasons for praying from Scripture.",
    mcq1: ["What does Paul promise to those who pray in Philippians 4:7?", ["The peace of God will guard their hearts and minds", "All problems will vanish", "Wealth will come", "No one will oppose them"], 0, "The peace of God will guard hearts and minds."],
    mcq2: ["What does God say in Jeremiah 33:3?", ["Call to me and I will answer you", "Be silent before me", "Do not ask", "Wait without speaking"], 0, "God invites the prophet to call on him."],
