    apply: "Begin each prayer this week by saying 'Father' slowly and thanking him for being your Father. If you struggle with the idea, read Luke 15:11-24 and picture the father running to meet his son. Write a short prayer asking God to heal any hurt linked to earthly fathers.",
    activity: "Read Luke 15:11-24 together slowly. Ask learners to list the actions of the father in the story. Then ask how these show what God is like when we come to him in prayer. Finish by praying the first line of the Lord's Prayer together several times, with pauses.",
    takeHome: "Read Matthew 6:9-13, Romans 8:12-17, Galatians 4:1-7 and Luke 15:11-32. Write a letter to God addressed to 'My Father', saying what is on your heart. Memorise Romans 8:15.",
