    apply: "When you pray this week, begin by thanking Jesus for opening the way and say aloud, 'I come to you because of Christ.' If you feel unworthy, read Hebrews 4:14-16 first. Ask yourself of each request whether you can honestly ask it for the glory of Jesus.",
    activity: "Draw a curtain on the board with a heavy line labelled 'Sin' and another opening labelled 'Christ'. Ask learners how the curtain was torn according to Matthew 27:51 and Hebrews 10:19-22. Discuss what it means for our confidence in prayer, and close with a prayer of thanks for access.",
    takeHome: "Read Hebrews 4:14-5:10, Hebrews 10:19-25, John 14:1-14 and 1 Timothy 2:1-7. Write a paragraph on why we can pray with confidence. Memorise Hebrews 4:16.",
